<title>JAPAN: NITTETSU BUTSURYU TO FORM THAI STEEL PRODUCTS FIRM.</title>
<headline>NITTETSU BUTSURYU TO FORM THAI STEEL PRODUCTS FIRM.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nittetsu Butsuryu Co Ltd said on Thursday that it plans to set up a joint venture in Thailand in October to distribute steel products.</p>
<p>The new firm, Siam Nippon Steel Logistics Co Ltd, will be capitalised at five million baht, or about 20 million yen.</p>
<p>The firm will be 49 percent owned by Nittetsu Butsuryu and the rest by three local firms, including Siam Steel Group International Co Ltd.</p>
<p>The firm aims to post sales of about 200 million yen in its first year of operations.</p>
</text>
